**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | Count | Key issues |
|---|---|---|
| High | 2 | (1) Flat R-1.7 insulation default for all 16 variants instead of per-zone-type defaults from ASHRAE 152 Tables 5-A–5-D. (2) No duct leakage class abstraction — leakage fractions are bare user inputs with no zone-type-dependent defaults. |
| Medium | 2 | (3) Seasonal delivery effectiveness multipliers from Tables 5-A–5-D not applied. (4) UnderSlab buried-duct correction factors (burial depth, soil conductivity) absent. |
| Low | 2 | (5) No explicit `ConditionedSpace` variant (handled upstream as DSE=1.0 short-circuit). (6) Naming inconsistency: `Unvent`/`Vent` vs ASHRAE 152's `Unvented`/`Vented`. |

The zone temperature formulas and thermal regain factors in `zone_temps()` (lines 192–323) were verified and are correct across all 16 variants. The gaps are in the three areas the review targeted: insulation defaults, leakage class assignments, and seasonal multipliers — none of which are implemented in the enum or the DSE calculation path.
